    "quote": "Let $\\delta<1/2$. Assume that $\\pp^j$ are reward vectors as introduced at the beginning of this section, where $p_i\\in [\\eta,1-\\eta]$ for some $\\eta>0$. Any quantum algorithm that identifies the best arm when it is known that the reward vector is in $\\{\\pp^0,\\ldots,\\pp^n\\}$ with probability at least $1-\\delta$ requires at least T\\geq c H(\\pp^1)=c\\sum_{i=2}^N \\Delta_i^{-2} calls to the oracle ... c(\\delta,\\eta)=\\left(\\frac{\\eta(1-2\\sqrt{\\delta(1-\\delta))}}{20}\\right)^2."
